.TH sync "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
sync \- flush system buffers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsync\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
sync -- flush system buffers
Usage:	sync
.HE
.B sync
calls the
.B sync()
system call, which schedules all in-memory disk buffers that have been
modified but not yet written out to be written to disk.
.B sync
then returns immediately; it does not wait for the writing to finish.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sync()
.SH NOTES
The system runs
.B sync
automatically at intervals, and as part of an orderly shutdown.
Running
.B sync
by hand before halting the processor abnormally (for example, before
turning off power) reduces the chance of losing data, but since
.B sync
does not wait for the writes to complete, running it twice, with a
short pause between, is safer still.
